1
00:00:01,780 --> 00:00:04,340
A product manager needs to understand some technical aspects.

2
00:00:04,340 --> 00:00:07,400
So during interviews, there are often some technical questions.

3
00:00:07,400 --> 00:00:08,950
Interviewers will assess the product manager's technical knowledge.

4
00:00:08,950 --> 00:00:12,270
Today, I've compiled 12 questions and answers for you.

5
00:00:12,270 --> 00:00:14,840
Just memorize them before your interview.

6
00:00:14,840 --> 00:00:16,400
The first question to prepare for is:

7
00:00:16,400 --> 00:00:17,680
What programming languages are commonly used in development?

8
00:00:17,680 --> 00:00:18,500
What databases are used?

9
00:00:18,500 --> 00:00:20,780
Generally, companies use Java.

10
00:00:20,780 --> 00:00:22,140
Of course, there's also Go.

11
00:00:22,140 --> 00:00:23,500
And some use Filipino resources.

12
00:00:23,500 --> 00:00:25,900
Others use C++ and so on.

13
00:00:25,900 --> 00:00:27,420
But the most commonly used is Java.

14
00:00:27,420 --> 00:00:28,140
For databases,

15
00:00:28,140 --> 00:00:30,340
it's usually Oracle or MySQL.

16
00:00:30,340 --> 00:00:32,200
But for large-scale cards, there might be some issues.

17
00:00:32,200 --> 00:00:34,280
Or financial companies tend to use Oracle.

18
00:00:34,280 --> 00:00:38,050
While medium or small companies generally use MySQL.

19
00:00:38,050 --> 00:00:39,510
So these two criteria

20
00:00:39,510 --> 00:00:40,770
if you're going to provide answers

21
00:00:40,770 --> 00:00:43,490
you can say that for our backend development, we use Java and the database

22
00:00:43,490 --> 00:00:44,510
is MySQL

23
00:00:44,510 --> 00:00:46,570
and the second one they will definitely ask about

24
00:00:46,570 --> 00:00:47,950
is how you integrate across systems

25
00:00:47,950 --> 00:00:50,060
for example, the procurement project mentioned in your resume

26
00:00:50,060 --> 00:00:52,760
how did you integrate the W Mac system with the finance system

27
00:00:52,760 --> 00:00:54,410
it's essentially API interfaces

28
00:00:54,410 --> 00:00:56,970
For the internal systems, I can use MQ

29
00:00:56,970 --> 00:00:58,560
or API interfaces.

30
00:00:58,560 --> 00:01:01,620
When integrating with external systems, it's definitely through API interfaces.

31
00:01:01,620 --> 00:01:04,319
What product work was done during the integration?

32
00:01:04,319 --> 00:01:05,059
Firstly,

33
00:01:05,059 --> 00:01:08,759
we need to incorporate specific project cases.

34
00:01:08,759 --> 00:01:09,820
You can tell them,

35
