48
00:01:33,750 --> 00:01:36,230
After the third product requirement review meeting

49
00:01:36,230 --> 00:01:39,180
the development, testing, and launch timeline

50
00:01:39,180 --> 00:01:41,080
will be communicated to all relevant parties

51
00:01:41,080 --> 00:01:43,370
to ensure they can coordinate their efforts

52
00:01:43,370 --> 00:01:44,210
Fourth

53
00:01:44,210 --> 00:01:46,030
if any issues arise after the launch

54
00:01:46,030 --> 00:01:48,370
I'll also determine whether it's an issue with our system

55
00:01:48,370 --> 00:01:49,820
or with the third-party system

56
00:01:49,820 --> 00:01:51,540
If it's a third-party system issue

57
00:01:51,540 --> 00:01:54,170
I'll need to communicate with their product manager

58
00:01:54,170 --> 00:01:57,490
This will be integrated into our workflow and specific projects

59
00:01:57,490 --> 00:01:59,390
to elaborate and provide explanations

60
00:01:59,390 --> 00:02:01,490
When I interface with the third-party system

61
00:02:01,490 --> 00:02:03,080
I need to figure out what needs to be done

62
00:02:03,080 --> 00:02:05,960
The interviewer will also probe deeper, saying hmm

63
00:02:05,960 --> 00:02:08,639
So, you've integrated with the financial system or the WMS system?

64
00:02:08,639 --> 00:02:10,410
Which specific APIs have you connected to?

65
00:02:10,410 --> 00:02:12,470
At this point, you can discuss further with him.

66
00:02:12,470 --> 00:02:14,350
For example, in the purchase order process,

67
00:02:14,350 --> 00:02:16,130
we need to place KWM4.

68
00:02:16,130 --> 00:02:17,600
To have it receive the purchase order.

69
00:02:17,600 --> 00:02:20,840
We also provide an API for WMS to call.

70
00:02:20,840 --> 00:02:23,080
We receive the results of the purchase order receipt.

71
00:02:23,080 --> 00:02:24,520
If there are any cancellations.

72
00:02:24,520 --> 00:02:27,040
