73
00:02:27,040 --> 00:02:29,480
The WMS will inform us whether the cancellation was successful or not.

74
00:02:29,480 --> 00:02:31,280
In the return process,

75
00:02:31,280 --> 00:02:32,400
we have various elements,

76
00:02:32,400 --> 00:02:34,420
which revolve around the process.

77
00:02:34,420 --> 00:02:36,080
The interfaces called by both parties,

78
00:02:36,080 --> 00:02:39,350
but the key point is the project in my resume.

79
00:02:39,350 --> 00:02:40,450
My PRD document

80
00:02:40,450 --> 00:02:42,650
I am very familiar with my system flowchart.

81
00:02:42,650 --> 00:02:45,960
This is what you should be able to explain clearly if you're not quite sure.

82
00:02:45,960 --> 00:02:47,580
Then you should remove the specific project.

83
00:02:47,580 --> 00:02:50,220
You can also go through this workflow once, and that's fine too.

84
00:02:50,220 --> 00:02:53,660
The third one is a common conflict issue you might encounter.

85
00:02:53,660 --> 00:02:55,020
So, how would he ask?

86
00:02:55,020 --> 00:02:57,920
He might say, 'Has the development team ever ignored your requests?'

87
00:02:57,920 --> 00:03:00,320
Do you have any points of conflict with the development team?

88
00:03:00,320 --> 00:03:03,540
So at this point, you can introduce the topic of requirements.

89
00:03:03,540 --> 00:03:04,700
If he doesn't take on my request

90
00:03:04,700 --> 00:03:06,080
Actually, this issue exists in every company.

91
00:03:06,080 --> 00:03:07,840
As long as you've been a product manager for three months,

92
00:03:07,840 --> 00:03:09,940
