For example, when we were working on version 1.0,

142
00:04:42,690 --> 00:04:45,220
What kind of issues did we envision for the business?

143
00:04:45,220 --> 00:04:46,720
The development team thought it wasn't necessary to add.

144
00:04:46,720 --> 00:04:48,400
So, what did we do after that?

145
00:04:48,400 --> 00:04:49,770
We designed the product solutions.

146
00:04:49,770 --> 00:04:51,570
When we worked on the marketing projects,

147
00:04:51,570 --> 00:04:53,250
the priority of requirements was the focus at the time.

148
00:04:53,250 --> 00:04:55,850
There were conflicts with the development resource scheduling.

149
00:04:55,850 --> 00:04:57,890
How did we handle it?

150
00:04:57,890 --> 00:04:59,270
This is the third point.

151
00:04:59,270 --> 00:05:00,650
Frequently dreamed about,

152
00:05:00,650 --> 00:05:01,710
The conflict between you and the developers.

153
00:05:01,710 --> 00:05:03,030
or the requirements from the development manager

154
00:05:03,030 --> 00:05:04,710
how B handles it

155
00:05:04,710 --> 00:05:06,630
at this point, you mustn't respond with

156
