00:09:02,520 --> 00:09:05,200
As well as the basic capabilities we collaborate on for its development

280
00:09:05,200 --> 00:09:06,680
For our own product

281
00:09:06,680 --> 00:09:09,760
The main functional points and the extent of the round interface changes

282
00:09:09,760 --> 00:09:10,910
And the number of interfaces

283
00:09:10,910 --> 00:09:13,870
We can roughly estimate the amount of development work required

284
00:09:13,870 --> 00:09:16,410
Secondly, when formally assessing the workload

285
00:09:16,410 --> 00:09:17,370
During the requirements review

286
00:09:17,370 --> 00:09:20,410
UI development, testing, and their testers

287
00:09:20,410 --> 00:09:23,710
The key personnel and supervisors will conduct the review

288
00:09:23,710 --> 00:09:26,040
I'll have them schedule it.

289
00:09:26,040 --> 00:09:27,400
Before the project scheduling,

290
00:09:27,400 --> 00:09:29,440
I will also communicate objectively with the developers.

291
00:09:29,440 --> 00:09:30,560
Regarding this project,

292
00:09:30,560 --> 00:09:32,770
we need to report to which management levels.

293
00:09:32,770 --> 00:09:34,370
If the assessment is not objective,

294
00:09:34,370 --> 00:09:36,630
management will also call us in for a discussion.

295
00:09:36,630 --> 00:09:37,570
If it’s reasonable,

296
00:09:37,570 --> 00:09:39,420
our assessment will be approved.

297
00:09:39,420 --> 00:09:41,820
If there's a situation where the evaluation seems unreasonable

298
00:09:41,820 --> 00:09:43,780
I would also seek more professional assistance

299
00:09:43,780 --> 00:09:47,040
from the team leader of the development group and the technical supervisor to provide support

300
00:09:47,040 --> 00:09:48,600
because this isn't something where the product team can just say

301
00:09:48,600 --> 00:09:50,280
you can finish it in a week

302
00:09:50,280 --> 00:09:51,500
Everyone's capacity

303
00:09:51,500 --> 00:09:52,900
but that's a side note

304
00:09:52,900 --> 00:09:54,440
this isn't what you tell the interviewer

305
00:09:54,440 --> 00:09:56,020
this is just to help us understand

306
00:09:56,020 --> 00:09:57,500
For instance, you, a senior developer,

307
00:09:57,500 --> 00:09:59,580
can finish what a junior developer might take a day to complete,

308
00:09:59,580 --> 00:10:00,740
in just three days.

309
00:10:00,740 --> 00:10:04,590
So, the objective estimation of how long a task will take to complete,

310
00:10:04,590 --> 00:10:07,110
is something that the technical lead or the team leader,

311
00:10:07,110 --> 00:10:09,150
has a rough idea about in their mind.

312
00:10:09,150 --> 00:10:11,590
If a team member's reported schedule is unreasonable,

313
00:10:11,590 --> 00:10:14,050
you can seek assistance online,

314
00:10:14,050 --> 00:10:16,470
that's after the third evaluation.

315
00:10:16,470 --> 00:10:19,180
I will also address the milestones you provide

316
00:10:19,180 --> 00:10:21,980
by holding weekly and daily project meetings to track progress

317
00:10:21,980 --> 00:10:23,710
and address any issues promptly

318
00:10:23,710 --> 00:10:26,710
to align with your workflow and process mechanisms

319
00:10:26,710 --> 00:10:27,970
and reduce

320
00:10:27,970 --> 00:10:28,630
in terms of development

321
00:10:28,630 --> 00:10:30,830
the frequency of schedule changes for a project

322
00:10:30,830 --> 00:10:32,760
that might mislead the product manager

323
00:10:32,760 --> 00:10:34,180
and the tenth one

324
00:10:34,180 --> 00:10:36,260
He occasionally asks

325
00:10:36,260 --> 00:10:38,300
When you integrate with third-party systems

326
00:10:38,300 --> 00:10:39,780
Have there been any anomalies?

327
00:10:39,780 --> 00:10:42,530
How do you handle these anomalies?

328
00:10:42,530 --> 00:10:43,770
In our company

329
00:10:43,770 --> 00:10:46,230
We categorize them into business anomalies and system anomalies

330
00:10:46,230 --> 00:10:47,410
Business anomalies

331
00:10:47,410 --> 00:10:48,270
This is a bit off-topic

332
00:10:48,270 --> 00:10:49,930
What do business anomalies refer to?

333
00:10:49,930 --> 00:10:50,610
Business anomaly

334
00:10:50,610 --> 00:10:53,530
For example, when I pass on to downstream the purchase of four from W

335
00:10:53,530 --> 00:10:55,110
The corresponding delivery order

336
00:10:55,110 --> 00:10:58,030
When I call the interface

337
00:10:58,030 --> 00:10:59,930
The value for my shipping compartment B hasn't been passed.

338
00:10:59,930 --> 00:11:01,910
The WMS system will definitely trigger an alert

339
00:11:01,910 --> 00:11:04,250
Saying that the value for your delivery bay hasn’t been passed

340
00:11:04,250 --> 00:11:06,570
including the total quantity of my product

341
00:11:06,570 --> 00:11:07,450
I passed 100

342
00:11:07,450 --> 00:11:09,450
The total number of detailed results is only 90

343
00:11:09,450 --> 00:11:11,490
The WM4 interface would also trigger an alert

344
00:11:11,490 --> 00:11:13,140
This kind of thing is called a business anomaly

345
00:11:13,140 --> 00:11:16,160
A business anomaly is content that the product team documents in the PD document

346
00:11:16,160 --> 00:11:18,800
We would trigger an alert for business anomalies

347
00:11:18,800 --> 00:11:20,360
We would use DingTalk for the alert

348
00:11:20,360 --> 00:11:21,320
Or send an email alert

349
00:11:21,320 --> 00:11:22,849
Another form is a text message alert

350
00:11:22,849 --> 00:11:25,009
The second thing we would involve is

351
00:11:25,009 --> 00:11:26,369
It's the anomaly in the system.

352
00:11:26,369 --> 00:11:27,849
What about the anomalies in the system?

353
00:11:27,849 --> 00:11:29,740
The development team will initiate a retry.

354
00:11:29,740 --> 00:11:32,220
If it still doesn’t work after ten retry attempts,

355
00:11:32,220 --> 00:11:33,780
an alert will also be triggered.

356
00:11:33,780 --> 00:11:36,380
Then the development side will first investigate what the issue is.

357
00:11:36,380 --> 00:11:39,760
If it’s a business-related anomaly, the product team will also step in to handle it.

358
00:11:39,760 --> 00:11:42,280
If it’s a system anomaly,

359
00:11:42,280 --> 00:11:44,800
the corresponding development team will intervene to address it.

360
00:11:44,800 --> 00:11:45,840
If he can't handle it,

361
00:11:45,840 --> 00:11:47,480
he will also seek the product team for coordination.

362
00:11:47,480 --> 00:11:50,000
These are our business exceptions and system exceptions.

363
00:11:50,000 --> 00:11:52,020
So, what does a system exception refer to?

364
00:11:52,020 --> 00:11:53,160
This is a bit off-topic,

365
00:11:53,160 --> 00:11:54,100
but it's good to know.

366
00:11:54,100 --> 00:11:56,200
A system exception occurs when I call an interface downstream,

367
00:11:56,200 --> 00:11:57,440
like receiving a shipping order,

368
00:11:57,440 --> 00:11:58,160
and I invoke it.

369
00:11:58,160 --> 00:12:00,020
It just didn't return.

370
00:12:00,020 --> 00:12:02,140
He didn't give me a response for over 30 seconds.

371
00:12:02,140 --> 00:12:03,700
When I tried again, there was still no response.

372
00:12:03,700 --> 00:12:04,980
I tried once more, but still no response.

373
00:12:04,980 --> 00:12:06,920
Or it would just throw an error.

374
00:12:06,920 --> 00:12:08,370
An error indicating a system anomaly.

375
00:12:08,370 --> 00:12:10,490
This isn't an issue on the business side.

376
00:12:10,490 --> 00:12:13,440
It's likely a problem with downstream servers or something similar.

377
00:12:13,440 --> 00:12:15,880
So we need to document and address it.

378
00:12:15,880 --> 00:12:16,960
But for this kind of issue,

379
00:12:16,960 --> 00:12:18,430
there are established procedures in development.

380
00:12:18,430 --> 00:12:20,190
Developers often overlook business anomalies.

381
00:12:20,190 --> 00:12:21,510
They have clearly informed you,

382
00:12:21,510 --> 00:12:22,430
your shipping warehouse is incorrect.

383
00:12:22,430 --> 00:12:23,510
something is off with your setup.

384
00:12:23,510 --> 00:12:25,430
you need to make the necessary adjustments first,

385
00:12:25,430 --> 00:12:26,780
before calling other APIs.

386
00:12:26,780 --> 00:12:29,740
However, system anomalies might be due to a timeout.

387
00:12:29,740 --> 00:12:30,460
The network is unstable

388
00:12:30,460 --> 00:12:31,880
Then I'll try you a few more times

389
00:12:31,880 --> 00:12:33,600
If it still doesn't work after a few tries

390
00:12:33,600 --> 00:12:36,700
You'll definitely need to get the R&D teams on both ends involved to investigate

391
